                  <strong style="color:var(--d-text);">Context.</strong> An early-stage SaaS team had outgrown
                  their internal dashboard — built fast, never redesigned, now the daily tool for their whole ops
                  team.
                </p>
                <p class="body-copy" style="max-width:100%;">
                  <strong style="color:var(--d-text);">The challenge.</strong> Dense, unlabelled tables and
                  inconsistent patterns meant new hires needed a week just to find things.
                </p>
                <p class="body-copy" style="max-width:100%;">
                  <strong style="color:var(--d-text);">The goal.</strong> A dashboard that a new team member can
                  use correctly on day one, without a walkthrough.
                </p>
                <p class="body-copy" style="max-width:100%;">
                  <strong style="color:var(--d-text);">Our approach.</strong> Designed a proper information
                  hierarchy and a small component system first, then rebuilt each screen against it — one pattern
                  per job, not one screen at a time.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <div class="laptop-frame">
                  <div class="laptop-frame__screen">
                    <div class="dash-topbar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
                    <div class="dash-body">
                      <div class="dash-sidebar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
                      <div class="dash-main">
                        <div class="dash-card dash-card--wide"></div>
                        <div class="dash-card"></div><div class="dash-card"></div><div class="dash-card"></div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="laptop-frame__base"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="content-photo" style="height:110px; margin-top:16px;">
                  <img src="/images/deck/dashboard-analytics.jpg" alt="Analytics dashboard close-up" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="footer-strip">
            <span>uiedge.in</span>
            <span>admin@uiedge.in</span>
            <span class="footer-strip__num">07 / 16</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================
           08 — Case Study 2 · Solution & Outcome
           ============================================================ -->
      <section class="slide-viewport">
        <article class="slide">
          <div class="slide-inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">08 / Case Study — SaaS</p>
            <h2 class="headline headline--md">One system, every screen.</h2>
            <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:24px; gap:44px; flex:1; align-items:center;">
              <div class="laptop-frame">
                <div class="laptop-frame__screen">
                  <div class="dash-topbar"><span></span><span></span></div>
                  <div class="dash-body">
                    <div class="dash-sidebar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
